# tools/gen/chapter/copy_sameness_witness.rish -- one fold, sixteen copies, no drift.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/gen/chapter/copy_sameness_witness.rish
#
# Round e6 - priority slot 6 - galls_law_graduation.
# The graduation audit found copy_disjoint reachable from fifteen module-local
# paths. Correction to counsel's first reading (20260729.204722): fourteen are
# SYMLINKS to the one canonical tally/copy.rye -- the tree already keeps sameness
# through the filesystem. Exactly one, mand/tally_copy.rye, is a real file and
# is therefore the only path that can drift silently. This guard makes it loud.
#
# That real file has since been linked, so the split the lines below once announced no longer
# stands: 20260908.075300 reads 23 paths, all symlinks, no real file and no drift. The dated
# figures above are testimony and keep every word; what speaks as NOW reads its count off the
# scan rather than out of this header, which is why the say lines below print the scan's own
# output instead of a number written here.

say "copy-sameness: Language EN -- one fold, many copies, no drift."
say "copy-sameness: Style Gauge, Meter -- the split is the scan's to report, not this line's."
say "copy-sameness: Lens TAME -- sameness asserted, never assumed."

let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/c/copy_sameness_scan.sh"]
say scan.out
assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "copy-sameness: a copy has drifted from tally/copy.rye"
# values_apart: the scan's status and its verdict key must agree. If they ever
# disagree, a sentinel was typo'd or a path changed -- exactly the failure the
# old text-only verdict could pass silently.
assert scan.ok else "copy-sameness: the verdict reads ok while the status fails -- they must agree"

say "copy-sameness: HAZARD, named on purpose -- every module-local tally_copy.rye is"
say "copy-sameness:   a symlink to tally/copy.rye, so a write to ANY of them edits"
say "copy-sameness:   the canon for every module at once. An on-touch edit inside"
say "copy-sameness:   one module home is a tree-wide edit. The count is in the scan"
say "copy-sameness:   output above; this line names the hazard, never a figure."
say "GREEN: copy-sameness -- every tally_copy.rye matches the canon byte for byte"
